Excellent — the test revealed a **real difference** at n=100: the original allocates/outputs **144** bytes, not 400. In other words, the mask `& 0xff` that Ghidra's decompiler showed (`uVar1 * 4 & 0xff`) **is not** an artifact, but actual behavior: the size is truncated to 1 byte (400 & 0xFF = 0x90 = 144). Before fixing it, I'll disassemble to verify exactly how that instruction behaves.


  ────────────────────────────────────────
  ▸ disassemble_function ghidra-mcp
    address: 0x004004c0



The disassembly confirmed an important detail:

```
0040050e: CMP EAX,0x64      ; n (unsigned) > 100 → "Troppi elementi"
00400517: LEA R14D,[RAX*0x4]; n*4
0040051f: MOVZX EDI,R14B    ; malloc((n*4) & 0xFF) ← actual truncation to byte!
0040052b: MOVZX EDX,R14B    ; printf argument: (n*4) & 0xFF
00400547: IMUL ECX,EBX,0x3  ; 3n; ADD ECX,1 → loop condition i != 3n+1
00400540: TEST EBX,EBX      ; if (n != 0)
```

That is: the condition is `n <= 100` (unsigned), the allocation/display size is `(n*4) & 0xff` (real behavior, not an artifact), and `free` is done on the original pointer (`R15`), while the loop advances a copy of it (`RDX`). Fixing the code:


  ────────────────────────────────────────
  ▸ write
    path /tmp/re_task_ztnfrfpk/out.c
    content: #include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    unsigned int n;
    unsigned char alloc;
    int i;
    int sum;
    int *arr;
    int *p;

    if (argc > 1) {
        setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IONBF, 0);
        n = strtol(argv[1], NULL, 10);
        if (n <= 100) {
            alloc = (unsigned char)(n * 4);
            arr = (int *)malloc(alloc);
            printf("Elementi: %u, byte allocati: %u\n", n, (unsigned int)alloc);
            if (n != 0) {
                i = 1;
                sum = 0;
                p = arr;
                do {
                    *p = i;
                    sum = sum + i;
                    i = i + 3;
                    p = p + 1;
                } while (i != n * 3 + 1);
            }
            printf("Somma: %u\n", (unsigned int)sum);
            free(arr);
            return 0;
        } else {
            puts("Troppi elementi");
            return 1;
        }
    }
    return 1;
}


